  "title": "Delhi SIR Controversy Sparks Public Audit, 100 Voters Found to Be Misclassified",
  "summary": "Delhi's Election Commission faced backlash over its handling of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) orders, with a public audit revealing 100 voters misclassified as absent, shifted, or dead. Congress criticized the EC for failing to uphold electoral standards and demand immediate action to address the issues.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "100 voters were found to be wrongly marked absent, shifted, or dead during the SIR exercise in Delhi’s Okhla constituency.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Congress accused the Election Commission of breaching constitutional standards and demanded immediate action to restore the eligibility of wrongly classified voters.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The public audit was conducted to address concerns about voter misclassification and electoral integrity.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
